// endpoint_select_response.proto — SelectResponse: move or clear the
// response-selection cursor for one workspace. FEED section.
//
// Reply-to-a-past-response mode. The user, in the input window's command
// mode, walks the ordered final-response rows (`C-p` = PREV, `C-n` = NEXT)
// and clears the selection (double-escape). The DAEMON owns the selection
// state per workspace — it knows the ordered final-response rows, so it
// COMPUTES the newly selected feedid (both directions start at the most
// recent and wrap at each end) rather than the client naming one. The
// resulting selection is PUSHED to the webapp on the feed watch
// (frontend.v1.FeedSelection) so the bubble recolors and center-scrolls, and
// is also ACKED here so the caller (Emacs) can track selection state.
//
// The client sends only a DIRECTION, never a feedid: the daemon is the
// shared source of truth, exactly as it is for the footer and the feed.

